WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.301
Where this lesson sits.

2
00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:11.053
Week 3 covers two of the three remaining makemore lectures: this one on activations, gradients, and BatchNorm, and next lesson’s “Backprop Ninja.

3
00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:15.835
” Part 5 (WaveNet) is optional and appears in the GoDeeper at the end.

4
00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:30.536
These two were chosen because they explain the things you’ll see in every transformer: why layers are initialized the way they are, why there’s a normalization layer in every block, and how gradients actually flow through tensor operations.

5
00:00:30.816 --> 00:00:36.597
The lecture’s theme is that a deep network is a long product of operations, and products are fragile.

6
00:00:36.877 --> 00:00:47.565
If each layer slightly grows the scale of its activations, the growth compounds; if each slightly shrinks the gradient, the gradient vanishes by the time it reaches the first layer.

7
00:00:47.845 --> 00:00:57.211
The fixes, careful initialization and normalization layers, are best understood as controlling variances, which is calculation you can do on paper.
